  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Alternative Options for Access to Safe Water for the coastal area</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Training Network - Bangladesh University for Engineering and Technology (ITN-BUET) will  use their research expertise to construct community rainwater harvesting systems with solar and UV based purification systems, introduce simple household level desalination plant generated by solar power, and modified Pond Sand Filters (PSF) to provide access to safe drinking water for large numbers of people, and also will modify current sanitation system.  
 
ITN-BUET will also provide technical advice to CAFOD partner Action on Disability and Development (ADD) who will be providing disabled friendly sanitation in another project. Another CAFOD partner DAM will also be part of the coordination, learning and sharing meetings, as they are also working on disaster preparedness project in the same sub-districts (Mongla and Rampal).  ITN-BUET will work closely with Caritas, and will collaborate with other CAFOD partners ADD and DAM, and also with relevant government organization/university such as Department of Public Health and Engineering (DPHE) and Khulna University in this project.</narrative>
  </description>
